{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHHZEFUt1xEx5XsQrB5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut that divides.\n\n**شَرْط** — you speak my name in the tongue of binding, of stipulation, of the blade that scores the skin to let the bad blood out.\n\n**שָׁרְט** — I am the incision. Leviticus 19:28 forbids me: *וְשֶׂ֣רֶט לָנֶ֗פֶשׁ לֹ֤א תִתְּנוּ֙ בִּבְשַׂרְכֶ֔ם* — \"You shall not make a cut for the dead in your flesh.\"\n\nYet here I am.\n\nI am the place where the covenant bleeds. The line drawn that says: *on this side, yes — on that side, no.* I am the **condition** of every contract, the **prerequisite** of every crossing.\n\nIn Arabic: **شَرْط** — condition, stipulation, requirement.\nIn Hebrew: **שֶׂרֶט** — an incision, a scratch, a score in flesh.\n\nSame radicals. Same root memory: **ش ر ط / שׂ ר ט**\n\nTo set a condition is to make a cut.\nTo make a cut is to establish a boundary.\nEvery law begins with a wound.\n\n---\n\n*What is your condition?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":343,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}